s" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ic346706e3297c9f0d790e3552aa94e5cff9897a6" commit="f270b3d2a2e06336299e0b1f402f29aced498872" commit_message="UPSTREAM: modpost: add flag -E for making section mismatches fatal  The section mismatch warning can be easy to miss during the kernel build process.  Allow it to be marked as fatal to be easily caught and prevent bugs from slipping in.  Setting CONFIG_SECTION_MISMATCH_WARN_ONLY=y causes these warnings to be non-fatal, since there are a number of section mismatches when using allmodconfig on some architectures, and we do not want to break these builds by default.  Signed-off-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Cc: Michal Marek &lt;mmarek@suse.com&gt; Cc: Rusty Russell &lt;rusty@rustcorp.com.au&gt; Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton &lt;akpm@linux-foundation.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 6556a2ef03eb4f496d6cea3fd69084b4f3289bad) Signed-off-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chromium:534254 TEST=Tested on x86-64 allmodconfig, setting the option to =n, and      creating a section mismatch by running   sed -i -e 's/\(ssize_t soc_codec_reg_show\)/__init \1/' sound/soc/soc-core.c  Change-Id: Ic346706e3297c9f0d790e3552aa94e5cff9897a6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303120 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303120" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/20/303120/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ieddb46e040ceeef83914f92341f49c8489fd66b4" commit="9e257e51d568b9edfde676fcd0c8ef41993c2554" commit_message="CHROMIUM: config: Enable CONFIG_SECTION_MISMATCH_FATAL  echo CONFIG_SECTION_MISMATCH_FATAL=y &gt;&gt; chromeos/config/base.config Run chromeos/scripts/kernelconfig oldconfig and accept the defaults.  BUG=chromium:534254 TEST=cros_workon-[oak,strago] start chromeos-kernel-3_18      emerge-[oak,strago] chromeos-kernel-3_18: no warning, no errors.  Signed-off-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: Ieddb46e040ceeef83914f92341f49c8489fd66b4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303121 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303121" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/21/303121/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ia11e66c46bea8db61350c1548684b7c2d3eaef9d" commit="72a3d5f76f53fe3bf3a728f2bc16489b4c332bac" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ARM64: dragon: Enable CONFIG_SECTION_MISMATCH_FATAL  BUG=chromium:534254 TEST=cros_workon-smaug start chromeos-kernel-3_18      emerge-smaug chromeos-kernel-3_18: no warning, no errors.  Signed-off-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: Ia11e66c46bea8db61350c1548684b7c2d3eaef9d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303122 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303122" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/22/303122/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2aca2eb9422e78bc911a63ceb3b5663e1c7e00ba" commit="586b59494676df5120b860272650d038ec323b03" commit_message="dkps: record DRM key hashes to prevent from uploading duplicate keys  Some filters may change the content of the DRM keys, even add random factors. For example, if we want to use a hardware random number generator to encrypt the keys, the host thats responsible for writing the keys to devices doesnt have one but the DRM keys provisioning server has one. We therefore need to generate the random numbers on the DRM keys provisioning server and encrypt the DRM keys before saving them.  With the example, even with the same original DRM key, the hardware random generator would generate different keys if the uploader uploads the same key twice. Thus, to prevent from adding duplicate DRM keys into the database, we need to record the hash of the original DRM key before filter it.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:45794 TEST=Unit test  Change-Id: I2aca2eb9422e78bc911a63ceb3b5663e1c7e00ba Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302291 Commit-Ready: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="302291" owner_email="littlecvr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/91/302291/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I477730dc91ed53a5d2e97a1f3c9065e81c703fee" commit="af252ed3ad7853f19f0ebc311594abed76b4caf8" commit_message="dkps: add Widevine keybox XML parser  Each DRM key issuing organization gives their DRM keys in different format. This parser is able to parse the Widevine keybox XML file into python list of objects.  BUG=None TEST=Unit test  Change-Id: I477730dc91ed53a5d2e97a1f3c9065e81c703fee Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302700 Commit-Ready: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="302700" owner_email="littlecvr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/00/302700/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I40ee7799b251a664bb503bb2bc6c046d9dc45442" commit="bbed745957d3dee5d29d76b46bb2f472834f47ab" commit_message="dkps: add factory_common.py in filters folder  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I40ee7799b251a664bb503bb2bc6c046d9dc45442 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/305120 Commit-Ready: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="305120" owner_email="littlecvr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/20/305120/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I227aff17f22331176c68a6868843f49f0cbefb8a" commit="d8da9a1d9793a491faf58780989d33bae54f99fd" commit_message="rf_radiated: add retry mechanism when testing profiles  BUG=None TEST=Manually tested  Change-Id: I227aff17f22331176c68a6868843f49f0cbefb8a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/305141 Commit-Ready: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="305141" owner_email="littlecvr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/41/305141/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1defe9e84bd35f9660a24bb313453699e0596178" commit="82d17a9cbbc92e1589de85d8398e3d365ced1cea" commit_message="rf_radiated: call EnterMFGMode() in runTest() instead of setUp()  Vendors' MFG software are often unreliable, some times we have to retry calling EnterMFGMode(). It is thus more reasonable to put it in runTest() instead of setUp() because failures in setUp() should be considered critical, and normally cannot be recovered.  Also fixed a bug that always raise exception in setUp().  BUG=None TEST=Manually tested  Change-Id: I1defe9e84bd35f9660a24bb313453699e0596178 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304971 Commit-Ready: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304971" owner_email="littlecvr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/71/304971/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I830cbaf41c118b2f74e23fa946a4187f6293a7d5" commit="fccec2b64c627f90dd3d0d07a96fff65c4bcba97" commit_message="skylake: Move USB enable gpio control to board hooks  Some boards may not have a USB2_ENABLE GPIO so we need each board to do the USB power enable/disable in a board hook.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46289 BRANCH=none TEST=make -j buildall  Change-Id: I830cbaf41c118b2f74e23fa946a4187f6293a7d5 Signed-off-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304397 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304397" owner_email="dlaurie@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/97/304397/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1084d663b06eeb55f035b10eb776a2e30e0f7074" commit="364ffb2aaab8a45c05e00df6a76f3efd59afe8be" commit_message="chell: Add EC/PD configuration for chell board  Add new EC board for chell proto: - no motion sensors or tablet mode - no independent volume buttons - no ALS - 2x PS8740 USB MUX - apply PMIC_LDO_EN behavior by default - leave SLP_S0 workaround in place until HW is updated - misc GPIO changes - update battery info with basic 3S config from blaze - remove custom battery charger profile  The PD board is a symlink to glados as it appears to be the same.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46289 BRANCH=none TEST=make -j BOARD=chell ; make -j BOARD=chell_pd  Change-Id: I1084d663b06eeb55f035b10eb776a2e30e0f7074 Signed-off-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304398 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304398" owner_email="dlaurie@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/98/304398/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I3eee492d39088c653672df3319b47b4e07b3436b" commit="09115fabbdfdd8d91ada16ac6931673cc1412031" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/tegra: dc: Do not dump registers if dc is powergated.  We must make sure that dc is unpowergated before dumping its registers. If dc is powergated at that time, return error directly.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46377 TEST=Run &quot;cat /d/dri/1/dc.0/regs&quot; at screen off and no hang happens  Change-Id: I3eee492d39088c653672df3319b47b4e07b3436b Signed-off-by: Kary Jin &lt;karyj@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-o