ug that prevents Chromium from detecting MIDI devices in some cases. The kernel fix is in these kernel commits: http://git.kernel.org/cgit/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/sound/core/seq?id=54841a06c54eb55918948c12ab9b5f02cacb6ab3 http://git.kernel.org/cgit/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/sound/core/seq?id=68ab61084de3220e2fb0a698c890ba91decddc85 http://git.kernel.org/cgit/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/sound/core/seq?id=d5129f33a0d155d69cb0652cfc87bbc4d132ca17  Instead of backporting the fixes, we can load this module directly to work around the problem.  BUG=chromium:499817 TEST=Boot with no MIDI devices attached. Go to http://webaudiodemos.appspot.com/midi-synth/index.html and connect a device. Verify that it appears in the MIDI_IN menu on the page.  Change-Id: I4eb4b849a9d72a800e462e92d58555897b50aacb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/276896 Commit-Ready: Adam Goode &lt;agoode@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Adam Goode &lt;agoode@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="276896" owner_email="agoode@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/96/276896/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Iac22a2ddfc04f07c83606a49a2a6225b90a372af" commit="1b50940693cb8e5d7bfe7b7a868ff2c4f4675f2e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: make x86 compilation succeed when CONFIG_ION=y  This is temporary, to unblock other work. There is evidence that this used to work on x86 (at least one shipped device) so we need to figure out where it broke and fix it.  BUG=none TEST=compiles and boots on x86 Signed-off-by: Luigi Semenzato &lt;semenzato@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: Iac22a2ddfc04f07c83606a49a2a6225b90a372af Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304863 Commit-Ready: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Luigi Semenzato &lt;semenzato@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="304863" owner_email="semenzato@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/63/304863/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6798f3a4eff67b747845c88a1fc1e759dc6cd678" commit="f0f3088132a9b753a260a613c2fc720b271739d9" commit_message="minijail: make it work correctly with shared mounts  This fixes some problems that appear when system booted with systemd. Systemd sets all mounts to shared. This means that when minijail0 creates mount namespace new mounts will propogate out of that namespace.  This change fixes that by setting all mounts to private right after creating new namespace. Also when remounting /proc it unmounts it lazily, as normal umount() may fail when shared mounts are enabled.  More information about shared mounts: https://www.kernel.org/doc/Documentation/filesystems/sharedsubtree.txt  BUG=chromium:537087 BUG=b:23496617 TEST=security_Minijail0 passes on lakitu_next  Change-Id: I6798f3a4eff67b747845c88a1fc1e759dc6cd678 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303158 Commit-Ready: Jorge Lucangeli Obes &lt;jorgelo@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Jorge Lucangeli Obes &lt;jorgelo@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Ulanov &lt;andreyu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Jorge Lucangeli Obes &lt;jorgelo@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="303158" owner_email="andreyu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/58/303158/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I59ae2851a0ba868816769021d9638fcb07206d28" commit="f6da2fe6c0cdb679a78fe39fb65abdb2a70389a7" comm